From 0bd9ac85b39872eb418d60de4a3378ad79aff7f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:15:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 104/114] core: expose the atom accessors external drivers need

ofono-binder-plugin reaches into a handful of atom internals that oFono
does not export: the assigned type and settings of a GPRS context, the
roaming policy, an SPDI lookup on netreg, PUK-to-PIN mapping, a full SIM
refresh, record-oriented SIM reads, USSD decoding, and the radio access
mode helpers. Add them, matching Sailfish's signatures and behaviour.

ofono_radio_access_mode_to_string() is deliberately not the existing
static radio_access_mode_to_string(). The static one renders combination
masks such as 'lte,umts'; the public one reduces a mask to its highest
single mode, which is what external drivers expect. Both are kept.

struct ipv4_settings and ipv6_settings gain a pcscf list so the IMS proxy
addresses a driver reports can be stored. The binder driver passes the
setters as function pointers, so they have to exist even though nothing
reads the value back out yet.

ofono_voicecall_ringback_tone_notify() is accepted and discarded: the
Sailfish VoiceCallAgent D-Bus API it forwards to is not implemented here.
See doc/ringback-tone.txt.

OFONO_GPRS_AUTH_METHOD_ANY is now handled in the five remaining driver
switches that enumerate the auth method. Those paths are unreachable on
binder hardware, but an explicit choice beats silent fallthrough.

(cherry picked from commit e7d66c54ab8ef49cdd49fc6c3131156cd8d1624e)
Upstream-Status: Pending
