diff --git a/doc/ringback-tone.txt b/doc/ringback-tone.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c9eb145
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/ringback-tone.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+Ringback tone notification
+==========================
+
+ofono_voicecall_ringback_tone_notify() exists so that a modem driver can
+tell oFono when the network is not generating in-band ringback and the
+device should play a local tone for an outgoing call. The binder driver
+calls it.
+
+In Sailfish OS the notification is forwarded to a VoiceCallAgent that the
+UI registers over D-Bus (org.ofono.VoiceCallAgent). That agent API is not
+implemented here, so the call is currently accepted and discarded.
+
+Consequence: on hardware where the network does not supply in-band
+ringback, an outgoing call is silent until it is answered. Nothing
+regresses relative to stock oFono, which has no such notification at all.
+
+Implementing this properly means porting src/voicecallagent.c and the
+RegisterVoicecallAgent/UnregisterVoicecallAgent methods on
+org.ofono.VoiceCallManager, and then teaching the LuneOS dialer to
+register an agent and play the tone. Both halves are needed; neither is
+useful alone.
